  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Reaction of aniline sulphonic acid with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaNO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi></math> gives diazo ester sulphonic acid. Which on further treatment with naphthalene derivative undergoes diazo coupling reaction to give red azo dye.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4794da58-c530-4672-ad6a-6a7ebfa24171.png\" style=\"width: 700px; height: 270px;\"/></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/2cca182a-c4db-4896-828d-ccf85b1c2e1e.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 530px;\"/></p><p>This is known as Griess-Ilosvay test. </p>",
    "image": null
  },
